Fix \(\epsilon>0\), \(\lambda\in[0,1]\), and an integer \(K\geq1\), and put \(D=2(K-1)\). Let \(c^0,R\in\mathbb R^{\mathcal Z}\) satisfy \(R_\zeta>0\) and \(c^0_\zeta-R_\zeta\geq0\) for every \(\zeta\in\mathcal Z\), so that the rectangle \(\prod_{\zeta\in\mathcal Z}[c^0_\zeta-R_\zeta,c^0_\zeta+R_\zeta]\) lies in \(\mathbb R_+^4\). Let \(P_\lambda\) be the tensor polynomial of coordinatewise degree at most \(D\) defined from \(f_\lambda\) of \cref{obj:def:dual-process} by the normalized order-four Jackson convolution on this rectangle, exactly as \(P_{j,\lambda}\) is defined in \cref{obj:def:jf-estimator} with the pilot center \(c_j^0\) and radii \(R_j\) replaced by \(c^0\) and \(R\). Then, for every \(y\in\mathbb R^{\mathcal Z}\) with \(|y_\zeta-c^0_\zeta|\leq R_\zeta\) for all \(\zeta\in\mathcal Z\),
\[
|P_\lambda(y)-f_\lambda(y)|
\leq32\{3(1+\epsilon^{-1})+1\}
\sum_{\zeta\in\mathcal Z}\left\{
\frac{\sqrt{(y_\zeta-c^0_\zeta+R_\zeta)(c^0_\zeta+R_\zeta-y_\zeta)}}{K}
+\frac{R_\zeta}{K^2}\right\}.
\]
